  <!--EN: Bitter espresso mixed with cream or milk, then further mixed with mint oil and garnished. Cool and velvety coffee gives way to an even cooler, soothing aftertaste, not to mention great smelling breath.-->
  <VBE_MintCoffee.description>苦味浓缩咖啡与奶油或牛奶混合，然后进一步与薄荷油混合并装饰。凉爽柔滑的咖啡让位于更凉爽、舒缓的余味，更不用说美妙的呼吸了。</VBE_MintCoffee.description>
  <!--EN: Drink {0}-->
  <VBE_MintCoffee.ingestible.ingestCommandString>喝{0}</VBE_MintCoffee.ingestible.ingestCommandString>
  <!--EN: Drinking {0}.-->
  <VBE_MintCoffee.ingestible.ingestReportString>饮酒 {0}。</VBE_MintCoffee.ingestible.ingestReportString>
  <!--EN: mint coffee-->
  <VBE_MintCoffee.label>薄荷咖啡</VBE_MintCoffee.label>
  <!--EN: Mint leaves are infamous for their cooling effect on one's mouth, as well as ease of seeping into an array of teas or delicately garnishing a dish. Mint leaves rot quite fast.-->
  <VBE_MintLeaves.description>薄荷叶因其对口腔的清凉作用以及易于渗入各种茶中或精美地装饰菜肴而臭名昭著。薄荷叶腐烂得很快。</VBE_MintLeaves.description>
  <!--EN: mint leaves-->
  <VBE_MintLeaves.label>薄荷叶</VBE_MintLeaves.label>
  <!--EN: A plant sprouting into an array of mint leaves. Mint leaves are infamous for their cooling effect on one's mouth, as well as ease of seeping into an array of teas or delicately garnishing a dish. Flourishes indoors and in plant pots, while being pleasant to look at.-->
  <VBE_MintPlant.description>植物发芽成一系列薄荷叶。薄荷叶因其对口腔的清凉作用以及易于渗入各种茶中或精美地装饰菜肴而臭名昭著。在室内和花盆中蓬勃发展，同时看起来令人愉悦。</VBE_MintPlant.description>
  <!--EN: mint plant-->
  <VBE_MintPlant.label>薄荷植物</VBE_MintPlant.label>
  <!--EN: Black tea leaves mixed with mint leaves and deeply steeped, then garnished with additional mint leaves. Leaves your breath surprisingly fresh.-->
  <VBE_MintTea.description>红茶叶与薄荷叶混合并深度浸泡，然后用额外的薄荷叶装饰。让您的呼吸异常清新。</VBE_MintTea.description>
